            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Insight 1: Regional Sales Contribution
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Observation:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> The West region contributes the highest share of overall sales (around 27%), while the East region contributes the least (around 23%).
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Business Value:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> Management can prioritize marketing and distribution in weaker regions (like East) to balance performance, while reinforcing strategies in strong regions (like West) to maintain dominance.
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Insight 2: Profitability vs Sales Relationship
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Observation:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> The scatter plot shows that some high‑sales orders are associated with low or even negative profit.
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Business Value:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> Finance can identify and review these loss‑making orders, adjust discount policies, and refine pricing strategies to ensure that high sales also translate into healthy profit margins.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.0745429'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.810127'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
        </annotations>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{10A11A5B-8472-4A05-A6C8-9AB751384AB5}' />
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Q9'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Q9.</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Æ </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Chart Selection Justification:</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Explain why different charts were used for different business questions in this analysis.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources />
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style />
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Automatic' />
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows />
        <cols />
        <annotations>
          <annotation class='area' id='0' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>1. Sales Trend Analysis (Line Chart)
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Why chosen:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> A line chart clearly shows changes over time, making it easy to spot peaks and dips in monthly sales.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Business value:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> Leadership can identify seasonal patterns and plan promotions or inventory accordingly.
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>2. Regional Contribution Analysis (Pie Chart)
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Why chosen:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> A pie chart highlights proportions, showing how much each region contributes to total sales.
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Business value:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> Regional managers can quickly see which region dominates and which needs improvement.
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>3. Profitability Investigation (Scatter Plot)
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Why chosen:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> A scatter plot reveals the relationship between sales and profit, showing which high‑sales orders are low‑profit or loss‑making.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Business value:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> Finance can identify risky orders and adjust pricing or discount strategies.
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>4. Category vs Region Performance (Bar Chart)
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Why chosen:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> A grouped bar chart allows comparison of product categories across regions in one view.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Business value:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> Operations can see which categories perform best in which regions, guiding resource allocation.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.00282087'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.99859'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
        </annotations>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{08013F04-B74F-4BCC-8782-A27849A38865}' />
    </worksheet>
